  "Name": "Yenisoy2019-Ge-MWIR-AR3-asbuilt",
  "Source": "A. Yenisoy, C. Yesilyaprak, K. Ruzgar, and S. Tuzemen, \"Ultra-broad band antireflection coating at mid wave infrared for high efficient germanium optics,\" Opt. Mater. Express 9, 3123-3131 (2019). doi:10.1364/OME.9.003123 - Table 2 (p. 3128), column 'Measured Thickness (nm)': 132 / 108 / 733 nm (layers 1-3 numbered from the substrate); thickness errors -3, +3, +8 nm in Fig. 6",
  "Notes": "Same AR coating with the measured (as-deposited) layer thicknesses\nSpecification: As-built version of Yenisoy2019-Ge-MWIR-AR3; each layer within the 3 % tolerance window (131-139, 102-108, 703-747 nm).\nReported: Overall stack thickness measured by optical profiler on a witness: 972 nm (p. 3127); the measured layers sum to 973 nm (132+108+733), consistent. Measured Rav 0.256 %, Tav 99.744 %, R 0.005 % at 3550 nm (measured at AOI 10 deg). Recomputation with these thicknesses (this extraction): R min 0.008 % at 3650 nm, average 0.18 % over 3400-4800 nm, 0.68 % at 3400 nm.\nNotes: Reversed from the paper's substrate-first numbering. Thicknesses were extracted from FTIR spectra by random error analysis. Paper attributes the sim/measurement differences to thickness deviations and AOI 10 deg in the FTIR.\nLayers from Table 2 (p. 3128), column 'Measured Thickness (nm)': 132 / 108 / 733 nm (layers 1-3 numbered from the substrate); thickness errors -3, +3, +8 nm in Fig. 6; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), differs from the paper: ours Rav 0.183 %, R max 0.68 % over 3.4-4.8 um; paper Rav 0.256 % (measured), R < 0.5 % throughout. The measured thicknesses with the printed dispersions exceed the measured 0.5 % only at the 3.4 um band edge (0.68 %); the measurement was at 10 deg and a nanometre of thickness moves that edge.",
